REM plan-123-B: a character the selected codepage cannot spell is REJECTED, not
REM substituted. U+4E16 has no windows-1252 byte, so this encode raises
REM ErrInvalidFormat (7-705-0003) and the process exits non-zero.
REM
REM The encode is deliberately NOT wrapped in a TRAP: the point is that the raise
REM escapes rather than a `?`, an HTML numeric reference, or some arbitrary byte
REM being emitted in its place. Substituting is a caller policy, and this call does
REM not make it for you.

IMPORT io
IMPORT encoding

FUNC main AS Integer
  io::print(encoding::hexEncode(encoding::codepageEncode(encoding::Codepage.Windows1252, "hi 世")))
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
